WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.068
-Hey, welcome everybody.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:04.337
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:07.373
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you so much for watching.

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:10.043
Well, let's get to
the news and jokes.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.211
Guys, everyone
is still talking about

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:14.914
Rudy Giuliani's
press conference.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:18.084
And, I mean, by now,
we've all seen what happened

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:21.588
with the hair dye,
which is still insane.

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:25.025
I still can't believe that that
was real, but it was real.

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:28.695
But something you
might have missed was

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.563
what he did with
his handkerchief.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:33.900
And this -- Just watch this.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.102
-That is true.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:38.037
It is somehow related to this,

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:40.807
but I do not know whether good
guys got it or bad guys got it.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.343
-So you don't know who hid that.

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:46.079
-Ugh!

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:48.414
Oh, my gosh!

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:50.549
-I can only hear
one person at the top.

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:53.352
-Oh, my...

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:55.220
Wow!

00:00:55.220 --> 00:01:00.126
I think Rudy's trying to
single-handedly start COVID-20.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.560
Seriously,
when it saw that clip,

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.796
even COVID-19
immediately put on a mask.

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.965
It's like, "Oh, gosh!"

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.834
If that's what
Rudy does on national TV,

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.702
I don't want to see
what he does at home.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:12.471
It's like...

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:13.639
-It got silent.

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:15.274
-Also, why do I get
the feeling Rudy

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:18.144
has been using the same
dinner napkin since 1974?

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:21.681
He's like,
"It's my lucky napkin."

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:23.816
Rudy's having a brutal 2020.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.517
I mean, a month ago,
he got caught on film

00:01:25.517 --> 00:01:27.386
sticking his hand
down his pants.

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:29.422
It wasn't even close to
his worst moment.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:33.226
I mean, not surprisingly,
today, it came out that Giuliani

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:35.595
and other key members of
Trump's legal team

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.863
have been exposed to
the coronavirus.

00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:39.365
But this is nice.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.100
Rudy is offering
to share his wet hankie

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.569
with anyone who needs it.

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:45.004
Rudy was tested,
and, thankfully,

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:51.176
the results were negative,
which raises the question, how?

00:01:51.176 --> 00:01:52.978
How is that possible?

00:01:52.978 --> 00:01:54.747
I'm going to the store,
I've got like 20 masks on.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:55.981
I'm wearing gloves.

00:01:55.981 --> 00:02:01.020
And this guy is rubbing snot
all over his face.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.788
Yeah, when they gave Rudy
the COVID test,

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:04.590
you could almost hear the swab
going, "No, no, no!

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:05.658
Don't stick me in --
You know what?

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:06.659
I had a good run.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.594
I had a good run."

00:02:08.594 --> 00:02:11.063
Speaking of the pandemic,
today, Pfizer announced

00:02:11.063 --> 00:02:12.432
that they have officially
applied for

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:15.301
emergency authorization
for their vaccine,

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:17.236
which means it could be
approved for use

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:18.938
as early as mid-December.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.206
-Ooh!

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.842
-Yeah. Apparently,
Pfizer saw that Rudy Giuliani

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.510
press conference and thought,
"We'd better hurry."

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.813
I mean, this is --

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:31.417
If there's one,
there's more than one."

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.619
I don't know how I feel
about an emergency vaccine.

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:35.053
I'm not sure I like
the feeling of

00:02:35.053 --> 00:02:37.457
someone running up to me like,
"Quick, inject this!"

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:40.559
"Thanks."

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:43.229
Well, earlier today,
Trump held a press conference

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.131
to talk about drug prices,

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.266
but he kicked things off
by discussing the election.

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:48.367
Watch this.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.903 line:0%
-Big Pharma ran
millions of dollars of

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:55.574 line:0%
negative advertisements against
me during the campaign,

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:56.675 line:0%
which I won, by the way.

00:02:56.675 --> 00:02:59.578 line:0%
But, you know,
we'll find that out.

00:02:59.578 --> 00:03:01.514 line:0%
Almost 74 million votes.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:06.119
-As soon as Trump said that,
the C.E.O. of Twitter ran in

00:03:06.119 --> 00:03:08.521
and said,
"This claim has been disputed.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.590
Keep going."

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.057
Trump still can't accept losing.

00:03:12.057 --> 00:03:14.927
If you're wondering why
we have participation trophies,

00:03:14.927 --> 00:03:18.363
this is exactly why.

00:03:18.363 --> 00:03:19.966
This is exact--

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:22.735
[ As Trump ]
There are no losers.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:25.138
We all won.

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:27.040
[ Normal voice ]
Trump was like, "74 million --

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.108
you round that up, it's
100 million,

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:30.876
which you can then round up
to a billion.

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:35.181
So, how about that, folks?
A billion votes."

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:36.849
Speaking of Trump,
I saw that judges in

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.552
Arizona, Pennsylvania, and
Georgia have all thrown out

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.387
lawsuits from
the Trump administration,

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.556
but he continues
to dish out more.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:46.626
I'm starting to think he doesn't
understand how the law works.

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.460
I mean, just check out
the responses

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:50.930
when he was asked
about basic legal terms.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:54.100
When asked what liquidation
means, Trump said...

00:03:57.904 --> 00:04:02.609
When asked what docket is,
he said...

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.445
"Those are Dockets."

00:04:06.445 --> 00:04:08.581
Next up, for habeas corpus,
he said...

00:04:13.385 --> 00:04:16.055
He kept going.
For mandate, Trump said...

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:23.128
And, finally, for precedent,
he said,

00:04:23.128 --> 00:04:26.565
"What I'll still be in January,
thanks to the billion people,

00:04:26.565 --> 00:04:29.468
the billion people who voted."

00:04:29.468 --> 00:04:30.803
Here's a big tech story.

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:33.906
Apple has agreed to pay
$113 million

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:37.442
for slowing down
old iPhones on purpose.

00:04:37.442 --> 00:04:40.480
Yep, nothing teaches a company
a lesson like fining them

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:45.318
.0005% of their total worth.

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:48.354
They'll never do that again.

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.989
-Oops.

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:51.657
-Oops.
-Oops.

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:53.793
-Oopsie, yeah.
"Yeah, Here you go.

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.695
What's that? Oh, yeah. Sorry.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:57.830
Alright, I'm sorry.
Sorry about that."

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.732
Finally, I saw that --
Did you see this?

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.801
A British magician just set
a world record

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.903
for performing tricks
in an interesting place.

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:05.338
Take a look at this.

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:08.808 line:0%
-A magician in England set the
record for the most magic tricks

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:10.709 line:0%
underwater in three minutes.

00:05:10.709 --> 00:05:12.444 line:0%
He had 20 tricks.

00:05:12.444 --> 00:05:14.980
-Yeah. You could tell
he was running out of tricks

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:18.785
when magic trick number 18
was just shrinkage.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.255
It's good that
he was underwater.

00:05:23.255 --> 00:05:25.892
He couldn't hear the kids say,
"We should have hired a clown."

